      ":question/problem": "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}x+(3)y}{4}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(- \\frac{7}{2},- \\frac{7}{2})$,$(\\frac{5}{2},- \\frac{1}{2})$,$(\\frac{7}{2},- \\frac{3}{2})$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(- \\frac{7}{2},- \\frac{7}{2})}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right)+(3)\\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right)}{4}=\\frac{- \\frac{7}{4}+\\left(- \\frac{21}{2}\\right)}{4}=- \\frac{49}{16}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(\\frac{5}{2},- \\frac{1}{2})}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)+(3)\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)}{4}=\\frac{\\frac{5}{4}+\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)}{4}=- \\frac{1}{16}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(\\frac{7}{2},- \\frac{3}{2})}=\\frac{\\frac{1}{2}\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)+(3)\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)}{4}=\\frac{\\frac{7}{4}+\\left(- \\frac{9}{2}\\right)}{4}=- \\frac{11}{16}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-27-topic-audit-2/group-1/staged-assets/17592186172038/hard/8edb0729ce023f7dbccf3242da29945b8bf8a264aba8b6039ab1696195b46cc5.png)",
