      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2})$,$(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2})$,$(- \\frac{5}{2},\\frac{7}{2})$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(\\frac{5}{2},\\frac{5}{2})}=\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\frac{\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)}=\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\frac{\\frac{25}{4}}{\\frac{5}{2}}=- \\frac{15}{4}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(\\frac{3}{2},\\frac{5}{2})}=\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\frac{\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^{2}}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}=\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\frac{\\frac{25}{4}}{\\frac{3}{2}}=- \\frac{25}{4}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(- \\frac{5}{2},\\frac{7}{2})}=\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\frac{\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^{2}}{\\left(- \\frac{5}{2}\\right)}=\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)\\frac{\\frac{49}{4}}{- \\frac{5}{2}}=\\frac{147}{20}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-27-topic-audit-2/group-1/staged-assets/17592186172038/hard/d7b339f4ff9962584b40670ba23b6f581259226e62990e334461892ff3c395c5.png)",
