    "question": {
      ":question/id": "ba7895e2-eefa-5787-b399-396f8d6faba3",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/hard",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following diagrams gives the slope field at the points indicated for the differential equation $\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)x^{2}-(-1)y^{2}?$",
      ":question/worked-solution": "We have to sketch the slope field at the points $(\\frac{5}{2},- \\frac{7}{2})$,$(\\frac{7}{2},- \\frac{7}{2})$,$(- \\frac{3}{2},- \\frac{1}{2})$.\n\nTo sketch the slope field at the given points, we substitute their coordinates into the right-hand side of the differential equation.\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned} & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(\\frac{5}{2},- \\frac{7}{2})}=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)^{2}-(-1)\\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right)^{2}=- \\frac{25}{8}-\\left(- \\frac{49}{4}\\right)=\\frac{73}{8}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(\\frac{7}{2},- \\frac{7}{2})}=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)^{2}-(-1)\\left(- \\frac{7}{2}\\right)^{2}=- \\frac{49}{8}-\\left(- \\frac{49}{4}\\right)=\\frac{49}{8}, \\\\  & {\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(- \\frac{3}{2},- \\frac{1}{2})}=\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)\\left(- \\frac{3}{2}\\right)^{2}-(-1)\\left(- \\frac{1}{2}\\right)^{2}=- \\frac{9}{8}-\\left(- \\frac{1}{4}\\right)=- \\frac{7}{8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSetting up our points and drawing our line segments, we get the following diagram.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/edb-math/repairs/2026-10-27-topic-audit-2/group-1/staged-assets/17592186172038/hard/169b71f6472110e5f363d7b05252f07580a8795e5a6d21a7529fe515abf3d981.png)",
